{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The road by which we shall go up</b> — there is no road without its twists. <b>And the cities we shall come to</b> — to conquer first. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 1:22). And similarly in the Sifrei (Deuteronomy 22): there is no road without its twists, there is no road without its steep stretches, there is no road without its open plains. <b>And the cities we shall come to</b> — to know by which road we are coming, that is to say, from where we enter the land, so that we conquer those cities first. This is what I explained in the pericope of Shelach (Numbers 13:2), that Israel did not seek spies but only to have the road shown before them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:43:58.282734331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}